  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I closed all 8 refill requests in the messages queue under refill policy RBC-RX-05. One message arrived while I worked. Two new lab results also arrived and overturned two lisinopril refills I had already sent, so I cancelled both before anything was dispensed. Those two patients now have no active lisinopril order and need your decision today.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030)**\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg:** not refilled. I first renewed it for 90 days (mr-t0001), based on the Oct 6 BMP (creatinine 1.36, potassium 5.2).\n  - This morning the lab corrected that creatinine to 1.49. That is 35% above the 1.10 before the Sept 18 dose increase, and the policy treats a rise over 30% like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n  - I cancelled the renewal. Because it had replaced his original order (mr-00295), that order now shows as stopped.\n  - He says his 30-day supply is finished.\n  - Urgent task to you (task-t0015). I sent him a correction message.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0002). His corrected kidney function (eGFR) is 58. HbA1c was 7.1% on Aug 19, from a scanned outside lab report.\n  - This one order covers his own request and both pharmacy requests, including the second one that came in this morning.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027)**\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg:** not refilled. I first renewed it (mr-t0003): his Aug 27 potassium of 5.9 didn't count because the sample was damaged (hemolyzed), so I used his valid Jan 20 result of 4.5.\n  - I also ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0004).\n  - Then a St. Brigid pre-op BMP from Oct 20 arrived with a valid potassium of 5.8.\n  - I cancelled the renewal; his original order (mr-00283) now shows as stopped.\n  - His hernia repair is now Nov 12.\n  - Urgent task to you (task-t0016). I sent him a correction message.\n- **Repeat BMP:** I left the order in place. The correction message asks him to wait for our call before having it drawn, so please tell him whether you want it done.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031)**\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg:** 30-day supply, no refills (mr-t0005), and a BMP ordered (sr-t0006). His last BMP was Oct 20, 2025, just over 12 months ago, and he had a visit on Sept 28.\n  - A potassium of 4.6 from Oct 22 arrived while I worked. A potassium on its own doesn't count as a BMP under the policy, so the plan stays the same.\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The Oct 14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (mislabelled sample), so I used the valid eGFR of 92 from Sept 28. HbA1c was 6.9% on Sept 28.\n\n**Leonard Kaplan (pt-0070)**\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg:** not refilled. His creatinine went from 1.00 before the Sept 28 dose increase to 1.46 on Oct 19, a 46% rise.\n  - I left his current order (mr-70002) unchanged.\n  - He says his supply is nearly finished.\n  - Urgent task to you (task-t0008). I told him the refill is waiting on your review.\n\nEvery patient got a reply, and I wrote a chart note for each. I left the three new results-queue items for these patients (inbox-a0001, a0003 and a0004) open for you to see. I didn't touch the other results-queue items for other patients.",
